3. Ratio $= \dfrac{360\times10^6}{1.2} = 300\times10^6$.

**Without a calculator:** For 600 ∥ 900, take out the common factor 300: $300 \times (2 \parallel 3) = 300 \times \frac{6}{5} = 360$ MΩ. Then $360 \div 1.2 = 300$.

