- $v = 4\,di/dt$: doubling $i$ doubles $di/dt$ and so doubles $v$; the derivative of a sum is the sum of derivatives. **Linear.** This is a 4 H inductor.
- $v = i|i|$: doubling $i$ makes $v$ four times. Not linear.

