', '**Idea used:** work backwards with Ohm''s law, KCL and KVL — see *Dividers → Finding an unknown resistor* (Example 7).

Let the voltage across the parallel pair be $4R$. Current in 14 Ω $= 4R/14$. Source current $I_s = 4 + 4R/14$.

